{"schema":"SDW_SCRIPTURE_CHAPTER_V1","revision":"52add6f41edc5dd9c21f65f02f933fbd1cec266285bee8bce249607475050398","canonicalSourceHash":"f9dfbce6dd2edfe4bb3b4690acd6622f392035be2b0349df98f3607f0a05f6c2","bookId":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verses":[{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":487,"verse_start":1,"verse_end":1,"verse_label":"1","text":"Then Job answered,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1540},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":488,"verse_start":2,"verse_end":2,"verse_label":"2","text":"“Listen diligently to my speech. Let this be your consolation.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1542},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":489,"verse_start":3,"verse_end":3,"verse_label":"3","text":"Allow me, and I also will speak. After I have spoken, mock on.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1545},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":490,"verse_start":4,"verse_end":4,"verse_label":"4","text":"As for me, is my complaint to man? Why shouldn’t I be impatient?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1548},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":491,"verse_start":5,"verse_end":5,"verse_label":"5","text":"Look at me, and be astonished. Lay your hand on your mouth.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1551},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":492,"verse_start":6,"verse_end":6,"verse_label":"6","text":"When I remember, I am troubled. Horror takes hold of my flesh.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1554},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":493,"verse_start":7,"verse_end":7,"verse_label":"7","text":"“Why do the wicked live, become old, yes, and grow mighty in power?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1558},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":494,"verse_start":8,"verse_end":8,"verse_label":"8","text":"Their child is established with them in their sight, their offspring before their eyes.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1561},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":495,"verse_start":9,"verse_end":9,"verse_label":"9","text":"Their houses are safe from fear, neither is the rod of God upon them.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1564},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":496,"verse_start":10,"verse_end":10,"verse_label":"10","text":"Their bulls breed without fail. Their cows calve, and don’t miscarry.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1567},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":497,"verse_start":11,"verse_end":11,"verse_label":"11","text":"They send out their little ones like a flock. Their children dance.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1570},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":498,"verse_start":12,"verse_end":12,"verse_label":"12","text":"They sing to the tambourine and harp, and rejoice at the sound of the pipe.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1573},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":499,"verse_start":13,"verse_end":13,"verse_label":"13","text":"They spend their days in prosperity. In an instant they go down to Sheol.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1576},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":500,"verse_start":14,"verse_end":14,"verse_label":"14","text":"They tell God, ‘Depart from us, for we don’t want to know about your ways.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1579},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":501,"verse_start":15,"verse_end":15,"verse_label":"15","text":"What is the Almighty, that we should serve him? What profit should we have, if we pray to him?’","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1582},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":502,"verse_start":16,"verse_end":16,"verse_label":"16","text":"Behold, their prosperity is not in their hand. The counsel of the wicked is far from me.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1585},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":503,"verse_start":17,"verse_end":17,"verse_label":"17","text":"“How often is it that the lamp of the wicked is put out, that their calamity comes on them, that God distributes sorrows in his anger?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1589},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":504,"verse_start":18,"verse_end":18,"verse_label":"18","text":"How often is it that they are as stubble before the wind, as chaff that the storm carries away?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1593},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":505,"verse_start":19,"verse_end":19,"verse_label":"19","text":"You say, ‘God lays up his iniquity for his children.’ Let him recompense it to himself, that he may know it.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1596},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":506,"verse_start":20,"verse_end":20,"verse_label":"20","text":"Let his own eyes see his destruction. Let him drink of the wrath of the Almighty.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1599},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":507,"verse_start":21,"verse_end":21,"verse_label":"21","text":"For what does he care for his house after him, when the number of his months is cut off?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1602},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":508,"verse_start":22,"verse_end":22,"verse_label":"22","text":"“Shall any teach God knowledge, since he judges those who are high?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1606},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":509,"verse_start":23,"verse_end":23,"verse_label":"23","text":"One dies in his full strength, being wholly at ease and quiet.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1609},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":510,"verse_start":24,"verse_end":24,"verse_label":"24","text":"His pails are full of milk. The marrow of his bones is moistened.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1612},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":511,"verse_start":25,"verse_end":25,"verse_label":"25","text":"Another dies in bitterness of soul, and never tastes of good.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1615},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":512,"verse_start":26,"verse_end":26,"verse_label":"26","text":"They lie down alike in the dust. The worm covers them.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1618},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":513,"verse_start":27,"verse_end":27,"verse_label":"27","text":"“Behold, I know your thoughts, the plans with which you would wrong me.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1622},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":514,"verse_start":28,"verse_end":28,"verse_label":"28","text":"For you say, ‘Where is the house of the prince? Where is the tent in which the wicked lived?’","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1625},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":515,"verse_start":29,"verse_end":29,"verse_label":"29","text":"Haven’t you asked wayfaring men? Don’t you know their evidences,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1628},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":516,"verse_start":30,"verse_end":30,"verse_label":"30","text":"that the evil man is reserved to the day of calamity, that they are led out to the day of wrath?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1631},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":517,"verse_start":31,"verse_end":31,"verse_label":"31","text":"Who will declare his way to his face? Who will repay him what he has done?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1634},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":518,"verse_start":32,"verse_end":32,"verse_label":"32","text":"Yet he will be borne to the grave. Men will keep watch over the tomb.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1637},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":519,"verse_start":33,"verse_end":33,"verse_label":"33","text":"The clods of the valley will be sweet to him. All men will draw after him, as there were innumerable before him.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1640},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":21,"verse_ordinal":520,"verse_start":34,"verse_end":34,"verse_label":"34","text":"So how can you comfort me with nonsense, because in your answers there remains only falsehood?”","is_omitted":0,"source_line":1644}]}